    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/SLU-Saint-Louis-MO/Premium-Sales-Manager_2026-09975": {
      "title": "Premium Seating Sales Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. JOB SUMMARY The Premium Seating Sales Manager will be responsible for maximizing sales and service operations for premium seating offerings at Chaifetż Arena for Saint Louis Billikens Men's Basketball. This role focuses on new business development for Men's Basketball, growing a personal book of business, and delivering excellent customer service while actively cross-selling across all product lines for ticketed Billiken Athletics events. Ideal candidates will bring previous sports sales experience, preferably with an inside sales program or equivalent high-volume outbound environment. PRIMARY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES Sells and prospects new season tickets, with a primary focus on premium seating and suite rentals for Men's Basketball Achieves and exceeds sales goals and productivity metrics established by the management team Creates and develops new business by regularly pitching prospective clients through virtual presentations, face-to-face meetings, phone prospecting, social selling, and group presentations at events Delivers excellent customer service and cultivates relationships with current and future fans Works all Men's Basketball home games and home games for other ticketed sports as assigned - entertains clients, pursues new business opportunities, and answers client service and sales questions Performs other duties as assigned KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Excellent relationship building and interpersonal skills, with the ability to interact comfortably and effectively with internal and external clients at all levels Internal drive to succeed as an individual while contributing to team success Strong organizational and time-management skills Excellent oral, written communication and presentation skills Accuracy and attention to detail Basic networking and relationship-building skills Ability to work effectively as part of a team Ability to self-motivate in a partially remote working environment Available to work flexible hours including holidays, evenings and weekends MINIMUM OUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree Two or more years of ticketing, sales, or related experience Experience with Microsoft Office and Google Suite products Valid driver's license required PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience with a ticketing system - Ticketmaster Archtics Function Athletic Support Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/SLU-Saint-Louis-MO/Director-of-the-Student-Health-Center_2026-09677": {
      "title": "Director, Student Health Center (Nurse Practitioner or Physician Assistant)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. Director, Student Health Center (Nurse Practitioner or Physician Assistant) Shape the Future of Student Health While Continuing to Practice Saint Louis University is seeking an experienced Nurse Practitioner or Physician Assistant to serve as the next Director of the Student Health Center. This unique leadership opportunity combines approximately 50% direct patient care and 50% administrative leadership, allowing you to maintain an active clinical practice while guiding the strategic vision and operations of a comprehensive student health center. As Director, you will lead an experienced multidisciplinary team dedicated to supporting the health, well-being, and success of SLU students. Working within the Division of Student Development, you will help advance our Jesuit mission of cura personalis—care for the whole person—through an integrated approach to healthcare, wellness, prevention, and student support. This role is ideal for a provider who enjoys both patient care and leadership and is looking for an opportunity to make a meaningful impact within higher education and college health. Why Join Saint Louis University? Maintain an active clinical practice while serving in a leadership role Care for a diverse college-aged and graduate student population in an outpatient setting Lead an established Student Health Center supported by experienced clinical and administrative staff Collaborate closely with Counseling Services, Campus Recreation and Wellness, and Dean of Students teams Influence strategic planning, clinical operations, and student health initiatives across campus Work in a mission-driven environment committed to holistic student well-being Competitive salary range of $110,000–$130,000 Comprehensive benefits package including health insurance, retirement plan, paid time off, and tuition benefits About the Role The Director provides strategic, operational, and clinical leadership for Student Health Services and Physical Therapy at Saint Louis University. The position balances direct patient care with leadership responsibilities that support clinical excellence, operational effectiveness, and student-centered service delivery. The Director reports to the Assistant Vice President for Student Well-being and collaborates with campus partners and healthcare providers to ensure high-quality, accessible care for students. Key Responsibilities Clinical Practice & Patient Care Provide primary care services to Saint Louis University students in an outpatient setting Conduct health assessments, physical examinations, preventive care, and follow-up treatment Support patient care management and complex case consultation as needed Collaborate with physicians, nurse practitioners, physician assistants, physical therapists, and other healthcare professionals Serve as an Epic EHR clinician, accessibility manager, and super user Leadership & Operations Lead the daily operations of the Student Health Center and Physical Therapy services Guide strategic planning, goal setting, and continuous quality improvement initiatives Oversee departmental policies, procedures, compliance efforts, and clinical best practices Manage departmental budgeting, resource allocation, and operational planning Monitor healthcare trends and recommend innovative approaches to student health services Team Development Provide leadership and support to clinical and administrative staff Foster a collaborative, patient-centered culture focused on service excellence Support recruitment, onboarding, supervision, and professional development efforts Partner with leadership staff to ensure effective staffing and service delivery Campus & Community Collaboration Partner with departments across the University to support student well-being and success Participate on relevant committees, leadership teams, and campus initiatives Collaborate with local healthcare systems, public health agencies, and community partners Oversee student health and immunization compliance programs Support campus health response planning and public health initiatives On-Call Support Participate in an administrative and clinical on-call structure that supports operational needs and student health concerns during non-business hours. Minimum Qualifications Master's degree in Nursing, Physician Assistant Studies, or related health field Licensed Nurse Practitioner or Physician Assistant eligible to practice in Missouri Basic Life Support (BLS) certification Five years of clinical experience, including leadership, supervisory, administrative, or program management responsibilities Experience working with electronic health records (Epic experience preferred) Preferred Qualifications Leadership experience in college health, ambulatory care, primary care, or student health settings Experience managing clinical operations, budgets, and personnel Knowledge of public health, healthcare compliance, and quality improvement practices Experience collaborating across diverse teams and stakeholder groups Function Student Support Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/SLU-Saint-Louis-MO/Assistant-Ticketing---Broadcast-Media-Manager_2026-09953": {
      "title": "Assistant Ticketing & Broadcast Media Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. JOB SUMMARY The Assistant Ticketing & Broadcast Media Manager is responsible for developing and maintaining strong relationships with season ticket holders, mini-plan and individual game buyers and all SLU Athletics constituents. This position is also responsible for managing the day-to-day operation of the ESPN+ streaming platform. This position works primarily with fall ticketed sporting events (Men’s Soccer, Women’s Soccer, and Volleyball) and winter ticketed sports (Men’s & Women’s Basketball). PRIMARY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES Provides superior customer service to ensure a positive experience for all our patrons Fields in-bound calls and emails for ticket sales and customer service inquiries Assists in the promotion, sales and distribution of season tickets, groups, partial plans and single game tickets Leads the interviewing, hiring and training of student workers on an as needed basis (including identifying, scheduling and training SLU student workers for ESPN+ productions including talent, producer/director, replay operator, graphic operator, camera operator and engineer) Manages the complimentary staff and donation ticket requests including fulfillment and documentation Performs various financial and operational duties, to include payment processing, financial reconciliation, ticket inventory management, invoicing and mailing fulfillment Follows and understands the streaming minimum requirements set forth by the Atlantic 10 Conference related to the A-10/ESPN media rights agreement Works with the Atlantic 10 Conference to schedule ESPN+ events in collaboration with ESPN Works in collaboration with various groups to create and distribute postgame melts of events Works additional athletic events as needed; stays up-to-date with emerging trends in streaming technology Performs other duties as assigned KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Strong knowledge of video production and social media Proven ability to work independently, prioritize, and complete tasks in a timely manner Excellent communication skills required for working with diverse groups Strong written communication skills; excellent organizational skills with accuracy and attention to detail Demonstrated appreciation for diversity and inclusion MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree Two years of related experience Ability to work non-traditional hours including nights and weekends; willingness to travel, as needed PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS N/A Function Athletic Support Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/SLU-Saint-Louis-MO/Executive-Director--Center-for-Advanced-Dental-Education_2026-09899": {
      "title": "Executive Director, Center for Advanced Dental Education",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. Executive Director, Saint Louis University Center for Advanced Dental Education Saint Louis University (SLU) Center for Advanced Dental Education seeks a dynamic leader for the role of Executive Director. CADE is one of the finest facilities for advanced dental education in the world and has a proud tradition of balancing progressive excellence with the highest standards and the compassionate service of our Catholic, Jesuit heritage. Our graduates leave SLU prepared to be astute and aware clinicians using an integrated, multidisciplinary approach to caring for craniofacial and dental patient problems. Patients in our clinics experience exceptional, innovative and multidimensional care with intervention of all dental specialties as appropriate, using the best available means in diagnosis, treatment planning, treatment technique and concept. CADE also extends its resources to the community to offer dental education and dental patient care to those in need. Oral health care is a vital and challenging part of overall health care. As biomedical knowledge grows at an explosive rate, our faculty, staff and students are dedicated to maintaining CADE's integral role as a major contributor to the overall health care system. The Executive Director reports to the Vice President for Medical Affairs and Dean of the School of Medicine. Organizational Context The Executive Director is responsible for 10 full-time faculty and over 30 adjunct and volunteer faculty.  Operations are supported by over 30 administrative and clinical staff. The Executive Director oversees the education of residents in one of four specialties: endodontics (6 residents; 24-months), orthodontics (42 residents; 30-months), pediatric dentistry (6 residents; 24-months), or periodontics (9 residents; 36-months).  Key Responsibilities The executive director of CADE is responsible for the management of the Center functions, including finance, education, research, and clinical services. Specific responsibilities of the role include: Leadership and Strategic Planning Provide visionary leadership to the Center, fostering a culture of excellence in clinical care, education, and research. Demonstrate, understand, and support the institutional mission, vision, and values of Saint Louis University. Develop and execute strategic initiatives to advance the Center’s clinical and academic priorities in alignment with institutional goals and objectives. Work collaboratively with other institutional leaders and colleagues to develop and advance the goals of the institution. Participate in strategic planning for SLU. Encourage and foster an environment of professionalism, collegiality, and respect. Demonstrate intellectual curiosity and creativity, promote and sustain a culture of inquiry, and value the scholarship of research and teaching. Demonstrate professionalism, acting with integrity and inspiring trust and respect. Promote an environment of success through recruitment and retention of highly skilled faculty and health providers. Lead recruitment and retention efforts for faculty and staff in alignment with institutional strategies. Clinical Oversight Develop and support a leadership team for the Center to ensure the highest quality patient outcomes, strategic growth, and operational efficiency. Cultivate a collaborative working environment between department faculty and clinic staff. Oversee staffing levels, workflows, and clinical activity to ensure safe, appropriate, and timely patient care at adequate volumes for revenue production. Identify and allocate resources to achieve the clinical mission. Implement evidence-based practices and quality improvement initiatives to measure and enhance patient safety, and outcomes. Ensure compliance with regulatory and accreditation requirements. Administration Manage and oversee the Center, including budgetary adherence and effective, sustainable utilization and stewardship of financial resources. Recruit and retain a full-time faculty that represents a spectrum of highly qualified academic dental specialists. Oversee the evaluation of departmental faculty and staff in the context of a clear and developmentally oriented set of performance standards. Monitor and oversee clinical activity of the Center to ensure adherence to administrative policies, external accreditation, and regulatory requirements. Communicate effectively with program leaders, faculty, and institutional and colleagues, including practice and health system administrators to keep them apprised of CADE goals, progress, and areas for improvement.  Regularly solicit and respond to ideas from these groups of individuals. Work collaboratively with the Program Directors on recruitment, personnel issues, and educational needs for all faculty in the Center. Recruit and retain highly skilled and motivated staff for administrative support; manage and oversee administrative support staff. Mentor faculty for success in the academic promotion process. Education Oversee and ensure high-quality clinical education for dental residents and fellows within the Department. Participate in resident education, acting as a role model of effective teaching and self-directed learning. Monitor program faculty scholarship activity, providing feedback and guidance. Foster professional development, career advancement, research, and mentorship for CADE faculty and residents Provide career support infrastructure and mentoring for post-graduate trainees with a focus on performance on national examinations and facilitating the transition into the dental specialty workforce. Research Monitor faculty research and scholarly activities to ensure alignment with the clinical focus and within the scope of each specialty. Ensure the Center complies with standards of research integrity and compliance. Promote interdepartmental collaborations in research. Executive Director Qualifications The Center for Advanced Dental Education seeks a candidate with a commitment to academic excellence, the highest level of personal integrity and ethical standards, and an established reputation for compassion, inclusion, fairness, and objectivity. The successful candidate will be an effective leader and respected clinician with demonstrated ability to inspire, manage, mentor, and develop an inclusive culture for faculty and staff. The successful candidate will be drawn to the University's Jesuit mission and values, including its commitment to social justice. The Executive Director (0.4 FTE) and faculty appointment are open to those with credentials that merit appointment at Saint Louis University at the rank of Associate or Full Professor. Education and Licensure Requirements DDS/DMD or equivalent and board certification in one of the Center’s four specialties. Eligibility for an unrestricted Missouri state dental license. Experience/Competencies Proven leadership skills in an academic environment, excellence in teaching, clinical practice, program development and experience in research administration. Effective use of strong interpersonal and communications skills that incorporate tact and diplomacy, and approachable leadership style. Demonstrated ability to create a culture of engagement, accountability and shared responsibility for patient safety and quality of care delivered. Ability to nurture and grow residency and fellowship offerings and programs. A commitment to wellness and faculty leadership development. A record of cooperative working relationships with colleagues including patients, administrators, managers, and other colleagues. Center for Advanced Dental Education (CADE) Overview The Center for Advanced Dental Education (CADE) at Saint Louis University is recognized as one of the premier facilities for advanced dental education and training in the world. Grounded in SLU's Catholic, Jesuit tradition, CADE is committed to academic excellence, innovation, compassionate care, and service to others. We prepare future dental specialists to become thoughtful, skilled clinicians who approach complex craniofacial and oral health challenges through an integrated, multidisciplinary lens. Patients who seek care at CADE benefit from exceptional, comprehensive treatment delivered through collaboration across dental specialties. Our teams leverage the latest advances in diagnosis, treatment planning, and clinical techniques to provide personalized, evidence-based care that addresses each patient's unique needs. Beyond our clinics, CADE extends its expertise and resources to the broader community through educational outreach and access to dental services for underserved populations. As oral health continues to play a critical role in overall well-being, CADE remains dedicated to advancing the future of health care through education, research, and clinical excellence. Our faculty, staff, and residents are committed to contributing to the evolving landscape of biomedical and dental sciences while upholding SLU's mission of service, scholarship, and care for the whole person. To learn more about CADE, please visit: https://www.slu.edu/cade Applicants must include: 1) a cover letter including a vision statement (3 page limit) 2) a resume/curriculum vitae You can upload these items on the third page \"My experience\" of the application.  To ensure full consideration, please submit all application materials by August 18, 2026. Function Faculty - Medical Administrative Appointment Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
